    "description": "The visitor begins inside the Door at the shared center. Up/down changes plane; around changes Dwelling; entering changes local center."
  },
  "principles": [
    "Every canonical Dwelling may become a local homepage/center when entered.",
    "The Axis remains the global spatial center even when a local Room becomes the viewer's center.",
    "Adjacency is graph-defined, not Euclidean distance.",
    "A Door may connect two Rooms that could not be adjacent in a literal building; the rotunda reconfigures around the current center.",
    "Existing HTML pages remain canonical content surfaces. The 3D House is a projection and navigation system, not a second knowledge owner.",
    "Every visual route has a text/list equivalent."
